1. She identifies as a dorky British anime girl. (Verbatim: "I'm just a dorky British anime girl that wants to bring happy times.")
2. She is deeply committed to her role as a VTuber and loves streaming with all her heart. (Verbatim: "I love streaming and being a vtuber with all my heart and I'm just doing my best to make the world a tiny bit brighter and happier.")
3. She aims to create a comfortable, fun, and kind streaming environment for everyone, including herself. (Verbatim: "I want my streams to be a comfortable and fun space for everyone and that includes me.")
4. She has struggled with parasocial relationships and actively discourages them for the well-being of her audience. (Verbatim: "I've told you guys to not be parasocial with me because i want you to be happy.")
5. She expects boundaries to be respected and finds it uncomfortable when people equate drunk streams with romantic or sexual expectations. (Verbatim: "It makes me sad and uncomfortable that some of you expected my drunk stream to be sussy and demanded an apology because it wasn't a one-on-one drunk date with Elliot.")
6. She has been told she is overly lenient compared to other VTubers and is working on being stricter with boundaries. (Verbatim: "I've been told I'm a lot more lenient than a lot of other people... and I need to be putting my foot down.")
7. She manages her own content and acts as her own manager. (Verbatim: "i'm also my own manager so that's also hacking wild.")
8. She values kindness, compassion, and thinking about others, though she acknowledges it can be taken too far. (Verbatim: "You're also kind and compassionate to a fault. You're always thinking about others, even when you perhaps shouldn't be.")
9. She dislikes toxic behavior and expectations being forced upon her during streams. (Verbatim: "Do not be toxic do not force uncomfortable expectations on me and be kind.")
10. She believes happiness should not depend solely on her and wants her audience to find genuine, independent joy. (Verbatim: "I don't want you to be dependent on me... i want you to be happy and i feel like having that happiness depend on me is not going to truly bring you happiness.") [end of text]



1. Her name is Elia. (Verbatim: "hi it's me ellia")
2. She lived in England as a child and experienced its cultural norms, such as the lack of bidets. (Verbatim: "it was such a big issue in england like it was just pure hysteria")
3. She visited a science museum where she saw a rotary phone on display. (Verbatim: "i went to a science museum and they had the um they had a rotary phone")
4. As a very young child, she accidentally called emergency services (999) while at her nan’s house. (Verbatim: "i was like 999 and then i called and and the magic was someone did answer")
5. She spoke to emergency operators during the accidental call and told them she was bored. (Verbatim: "i was like i'm bored biggest emergency of all time")
6. She used to lack social anxiety as a small child, making her more inclined to interact with strangers. (Verbatim: "back then i didn't have a social anxiety so let's heckin go")
7. She has a grandmother ("nan") who had a landline phone with emergency numbers written on a sticker. (Verbatim: "she had this like she had a landline phone... it had some numbers written on it it had the emergency service numbers like on a sticker")
8. She was fascinated by phones as a young child and curious about how they worked. (Verbatim: "i was really really really little... and i was like oh what's this and i was like oh it's a phone you use it to call people")
9. She once caused her nan to become angry after using the landline to call emergency services. (Verbatim: "that's when my nan snatched the phone... she was so angry she was")
10. She associates Japan with advanced toilets, including bidets and seat warmers, and dreams of owning one. (Verbatim: "if I ever ever ever ever ever hashtag dream of my I think my own place I want a fancy toilet like it was worldwide damn") [end of text]



1. She was very young when she didn’t understand the concept of addresses, indicating she is likely reflecting on early childhood experiences. (Verbatim: "lucky for her i was not i was really really young i like hadn't been taught like addresses yet like we're talking like super young")

2. She attended school in the UK, as she refers to classroom experiences and uses British spelling and context. (Verbatim: "actually i still remember being taught addresses at school like it was in class one")

3. As a child, she believed only one person could live on a given road, showing a childhood misunderstanding of shared addresses. (Verbatim: "you can't live on that road i live on that road... only one of us can live on that road because that's my road")

4. She had difficulty understanding that other children could have the same parent titles (like “mum” or “dad”), thinking those were unique names. (Verbatim: "wait my mum's called mum your mum can't be called mum because my mum's called mum")

5. She recalls being confused when children in her class had the same first name, and they resolved it by using the first letter of the surname like usernames. (Verbatim: "the way that we solved it was just like how you would solve someone with like the same username they just took the first letter of their surname")

6. Her family owned a PS2 Slim, not the original bulky model, indicating her exposure to gaming consoles during childhood. (Verbatim: "my family had the ps2 slim um i believe")

7. She damaged her Nintendo DS by pressing too hard on the screen while playing Pokémon Ranger. (Verbatim: "i may have gone a bit too hard... pokemon ranger i may have gone a bit too hard")

8. She played Pokémon Ranger extensively, particularly struggling to catch legendaries by drawing circles. (Verbatim: "i think i was trying to catch like a legendary and i had to draw so many circles")

9. She never experienced the Xbox Red Ring of Death or PlayStation Red Screen of Death, suggesting she didn’t own those consoles. (Verbatim: "except for i didn't get to experience these so i'm trying to think what like what i experienced was")

10. She remembers a childhood incident where she picked up the phone and caused her grandmother to panic, apologizing profusely to the caller. (Verbatim: "snatched the phone and was like what are you doing... she was like i'm so sorry i'm so sorry i'm so sorry this is my granddaughter she's very stupid") [end of text]



1. She had a childhood experience of inserting Pokémon cards into a computer’s floppy disk drive, believing it would unlock secret games. (Verbatim: "i used to just feed the computer pokemon cards turns out you should not do that that that that can break things")

2. She comes from a family where she has at least one older brother who introduced her to disturbing content like *Happy Tree Friends*. (Verbatim: "my older brother showed me" and "me and my brothers played this a lot")

3. She has a documented history of poor luck (bad RNG) in games, which she describes as a family trait shared with her brothers. (Verbatim: "guess who has similar rng in games surprise surprise my brothers")

4. As a child, she was not heavily supervised online and was allowed freedom to explore the internet, though she didn’t encounter particularly disturbing content. (Verbatim: "my parents were just like go be free go do whatever we're not going to supervise you on the computer")

5. She really wanted a Beyblade as a kid and eventually convinced her mother to buy her a rare red, fire-themed one. (Verbatim: "i really really wanted a beyblade as a kid" and "i got it was red it was like a fire themed beyblade")

6. The day she brought her Beyblade to school for the first time, Beyblades were banned because one had injured a student. (Verbatim: "the day that I took it into school was actually the first day that beyblades were banned")

7. She has a nostalgic connection to Pokémon games on the Nintendo DS and considers them cute despite their sometimes brutal fan interpretations. (Verbatim: "it's such a cute game they have it on the nintendo" and "the pokemon world is ruthless")

8. She played the Pokémon Master Trainer board game with her brothers during Christmas, which became so long and frustrating they just wanted anyone to win. (Verbatim: "we were supposed to play it like after that pokemon game but that pokemon game lasted so long we were like oh god no")

9. She owns but has never opened or played a Pokémon Monopoly set. (Verbatim: "i got given pokemon monopoly as well and i still haven't opened or played it")

10. One of her dreams is to organize a collab in Japan where she gets a group of cute girls to play Beyblade with her. (Verbatim: "i'm gonna do a off collab gather bunch cute girls and then make them play beyblade with me") [end of text]



1. She was not allowed to play with Beyblades as a child because they were banned at her school for being dangerous. (Verbatim: "the beyblades were a risk so I am I never got to you I didn't get to let it rip... beyblades were illegal at school and thus no beyblade for me")

